# Operator-owned protected paths.
#
# See governance/GATE_MANIFEST_INTEGRITY.md. This file is the control that actually enforces the
# governance invariant "the actor being constrained cannot modify the authoritative object that
# defines the constraint" -- CI checks are detection, merge authority is enforcement.
#
# CODEOWNERS only has teeth when branch protection on `main` has "Require review from Code Owners"
# enabled. A CODEOWNERS file with that setting off is decoration; G1's DoD requires evidence that
# it is actually on.

# Governance state: manifests and approvals define what a gate may do.
/governance/gate-manifests/     @xLZDx
/governance/operator-approvals/ @xLZDx

# CI cannot police its own definition: for `pull_request` events GitHub runs the workflow as it
# exists in the PR's merge commit, so a PR that edits these files edits the checks that police it.
/.github/                       @xLZDx

# Policy-sensitive files (TDD 57(13)).
/core/SOURCE_POLICY.md          @xLZDx
/core/DATA_RETENTION_POLICY.md  @xLZDx
/core/adr/                      @xLZDx

# The operating contracts themselves.
/CLAUDE.md                      @xLZDx
/AGENTS.md                      @xLZDx
